<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Edwin von Manteuffel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1809">1809</a>–<a href="/years/1885">1885</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Edwin von Manteuffel was a Prussian field marshal who commanded armies in the wars of 1866 and 1870–1871 and led the German occupation forces in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> until 1873. In 1879 he became the first imperial governor (Statthalter) of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace-lorraine">Alsace-Lorraine</a> in Strasbourg, where he tried, with limited success, to win over local notables.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/edwin-von-manteuffel.jpg" alt="Edwin von Manteuffel" width="320" height="481" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Studio of Adolphe Braun · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edwin_Freiherr_von_Manteuffel_by_Adolphe_Braun.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
